  "interpretation": "Each imaging leg (BASS+MzLS, DECaLS, DES) clusters in a distinct sky region and carries a small per-leg CW-fraction shift from the global mean (~0.001 each leg). The leg-uniform asymmetry-field offset 2*\u0394f_L, projected onto the canonical mask via the leg-indicator field's l=1 sky-harmonic amplitude, produces an induced l=1 chirality contribution. The total summed across the 3 legs is 1.775e-03; the observed canonical-mask l=1 chirality amplitude is 7.040e-03. The induced morphology-proxy contribution accounts for 25.2% of the observed l=1 amplitude under the leg-stratification working hypothesis.",
